Solution:
cd client-app
git init
echo "hi" >index.html
echo "hi" >app.js
git add index.html app.js
git commit -m "Initial client files"
git remote add origin https://github.com/startup/client-app.git
git push -u origin main
git log

Approach:
1.as mentioned in the question change directory to client-app
2.then initialise git using git init
3.add text to the each file mentioned
4.then stage them using git add and file name
5.add commit 
6. will register the remote for the first time using remote add origin
7.push that using git push origin main
8.we will see what we have done using git log.